  "live_records": {
    "q-34073": {
      "dom_id": "step-q34073",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $Q(0,5,2)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,2,3⟩=16$, find the shortest distance from $P(1,-4,5)$ to $Π.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨0,5,2⟩-⟨1,-4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,9,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-6,2,3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-6)+9\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+18-9|}{\\sqrt{36+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|15|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
